  "_artefact_committed_at_note": "The simulation-repo commit this staged SET is current as of -- the last commit to touch this directory. Not `source_commit`, which in the four asset pins means the commit a VENDOR TOOL READ to produce derived bytes; nothing is derived here, these are the committed bytes staged unchanged. THE SEVEN FILES SHARE ONE LAST-TOUCHING COMMIT AGAIN, and the warning that stood here said they did not. Re-measured at this re-cut: `git log -1` names ceb4a0af for each of the seven separately. The split that warning recorded was real and is now history -- at §25 backlog 732's tree the four folds and palette.json were last touched at `a32ccf07` (§25 backlog 730) and render.json and centres.json at `82ede131` -- and it ended because owner ruling 2140 accepted a regeneration that rewrote all seven in one commit. THE PARAGRAPH SURVIVES RATHER THAN BEING DELETED because the distinction it was written to teach is what makes this field readable: provenance and checkability are different questions, the single commit above answers only the second, and the next time a backlog rewrites some of these files and not others a reader who assumed one commit authored all seven would be wrong again.",
